  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women Entrepreneurs Burao</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Burao, women play a central role in the informal economy, operating an estimated 65% of small businesses across Somaliland. Despite their economic role, they face persistent structural exclusion from financial systems, market infrastructure, skills development, and business support services. Social norms and unpaid care responsibilities (elders, etc.) further restrict mobility, working hours, and participation in training or business development. As a pilot and a feasibility study, a group of women market stallholders in Burao is trained, coached and facilitated in networking to improve their business and assist each other in being included in the relevant financial and the political marketplace.</narrative>
  </description>
